# Node step instructions authoring

Step files describe **traffic at one node** while the visit is opened. The engine already ran hooks and assembled the context packet.

## Steward loading

Stewards load context with `run context --markdown` — a **single markdown packet** with reads, allow grants, worker binding, **operations** (deterministic YAML), and **judgment** markdown. Do not separately read `instructions_path` or `operations_path` after loading the packet.

Step judgment is authored at `.cursor/foundry/nodes/{node-id}/judgment.md` (referenced as `instructions` in factory-flow). Deterministic steps are declared in `operations.yaml` when the node is split. Legacy `instructions.md` is deprecated for split nodes.

## Required shape

```markdown
# <Title>

## Goal
[Single outcome — artifacts/evidence only; no routing target]

## While opened
[Ordered steps; foundry-invoke fences for CLI]

## Boundaries
[3–5 bullets — prohibitions in plain language; no catalog check ids]
```

No header linking to `factory-flow.yaml` — the markdown context packet is the runtime contract.

## Rules

1. **Length budget** — ≤ 80 lines. Prefer schema references over inline field recipes.
2. **Assume context is loaded** — the steward already has the markdown packet; no `run context` in the step file.
3. **No routing targets** — no next-node ids, no `recommended_next_state`, no "prepare for shape.examine".
4. **No engine narration** — no lifecycle, hooks, or registry file links.
5. **`foundry-invoke` only** for Foundry CLI; placeholders `{run_id}`, `{visit_id}` from the packet.
6. **`ledger show` (intake only)** — on nodes that seal `intake-receipt`, use only documented flags (`--run`, `--from-seq`, `--to-seq`, `--types`, `--json`). Filter events to `{visit_id}` in assembly — no `--visit`. Agent-receipt step nodes do not use `ledger show` in step instructions.
7. **Worker inputs explicit** — table of Task launch fields from the context packet.
8. **Evidence order** — worker (when bound) → assemble receipt drafts from worker or steward outputs → write artifacts from worker → publish → seal receipts → `transition`. On intake nodes only, insert `ledger show` before assembling `intake-receipt` drafts.
9. **Receipt assembly** — point to `registry:schemas/...`; do not inline UUID/timestamp recipes.
10. **Intake `checks[]` (intake only)** — on nodes that seal `intake-receipt`, build `checks[]` from ledger `check.recorded` for this visit; do not pass `checks[]` to the worker. Agent-receipt step nodes assemble `agent.json` from worker or steward outputs only.
11. **Every branch gets fences** — blocked and proceed paths each show applicable `receipt seal` / `artifact publish` / `transition` lines.
12. **After transition** — not in the step file; reload with `run context --markdown` for the next node elsewhere.

## Shape intake (`shape.intake` — engine-owned)

| Owner | Responsibility |
|---|---|
| Engine | `visit intake complete` (or `run advance` when `config.shape.work_prompt` is set): ticket artifact, intake + agent receipts, seal, transition on pass |
| Steward | Capture `work_prompt` verbatim in chat; call `visit intake complete --work-prompt`; optional `visit state patch` for `app_folder` |

No step judgment file at this node. Do not `artifact.publish` or `visit transition` on intake — capabilities are not granted.

## Shape examination (`shape.examine` — judgment + engine complete)

| Owner | Responsibility |
|---|---|
| Model | Structured examination result via `shape.examine` task (`judgment.md`) |
| Steward | `run agent submit`; `answer` for clarifying questions; `visit examine complete` or `run advance` when no open questions |
| Engine | `apply_examination_result`, clarifying loop, agent receipt seal, transition, routing to present or `shape.examine.gate` |

No `ledger show`, `receipt seal`, `visit transition`, or `visit state patch` for examination domain fields on this node — capabilities are not granted.

## Shape presentation (`shape.present` — judgment + engine complete)

| Owner | Responsibility |
|---|---|
| Model | Structured presentation result via `shape.present` task (`judgment.md`) |
| Steward | `run agent submit`; `visit present complete` or `run advance` after PROCEED |
| Engine | Publish `presentation` artifact, patch `presented_ac`, agent receipt seal, transition to `shape.present.gate` |

BLOCKED verdict: engine seals agent receipt on submit only; no publish or transition until a later PROCEED submit and complete.

No `ledger show`, `artifact publish`, `receipt seal`, `visit transition`, or `visit state patch` on this node — capabilities are not granted.

## Shape record (`shape.record` — judgment + engine complete)

| Owner | Responsibility |
|---|---|
| Model | Structured record result via `shape.record` task (`judgment.md`) |
| Steward | `run agent submit`; `visit record complete` or `run advance` after PROCEED |
| Engine | Publish `plan` artifact, patch `approved_ac` fields, mirror `workspace:plan.md`, agent receipt seal, transition to `shape.record.gate` |

BLOCKED verdict: engine seals agent receipt on submit only; no publish or transition until a later PROCEED submit and complete.

No `ledger show`, `artifact publish`, `receipt seal`, `visit transition`, or `visit state patch` on this node — capabilities are not granted.

## Shape present gate (`shape.present.gate` — user decider, no worker)

| Owner | Responsibility |
|---|---|
| User | Semantic reject or accept after reviewing plan and presented AC |
| Steward | Turn 1: header, `## Plan presentation` body, verbatim `presented_ac`, STOP; Turn 2: `gate decide` with `produces.options` |
| Engine | `prior-present-sealed`, `gate.presented`, seal and route by `on.decisions` |

No worker, no `judgment.md` — gate instructions only (`instructions.md`). Presentation markdown is inlined in the markdown context packet; JSON context resolves `reads.artifacts` to `resolved_uri` / `resolved_path`.

## Shape record gate (`shape.record.gate` — user decider, no worker)

| Owner | Responsibility |
|---|---|
| User | Semantic accept or hold after reviewing living plan and approved AC |
| Steward | Turn 1: header, `## Living plan` body, verbatim `approved_ac`, STOP; Turn 2: `gate decide` with `produces.options` |
| Engine | `prior-shape-record-sealed`, `approved-ac-recorded`, `gate.presented`, seal and route by `on.decisions` |

No worker, no `judgment.md` — gate instructions only (`instructions.md`). Plan markdown is inlined in the markdown context packet; JSON context resolves `reads.artifacts` to `resolved_uri` / `resolved_path`.

## Execute start (`execute.start` — user decider, no worker)

| Owner | Responsibility |
|---|---|
| User | Explicit authorization to begin Execute (feature branch + `foundry start`) |
| Steward | Turn 1: header, `## Living plan` body, verbatim `approved_ac`, STOP; Turn 2: `start` after explicit confirmation |
| Engine | `prior-shape-record-sealed`, `approved-ac-recorded`, decision wait, `execute.authorization.recorded`, seal and route to `execute.intake` |

No worker, no `judgment.md` — gate instructions only (`instructions.md`). Do not use `gate decide` on this node. Plan markdown is inlined in the markdown context packet.

## Execute intake (`execute.intake` — engine-owned)

| Owner | Responsibility |
|---|---|
| Engine | `on_examine` + `on_open` checks; `run_execute_intake_complete` on `run advance` when opened: frozen shape validation, assessment, intake + agent receipts, transition on pass |
| Steward | Ensure clean git before admit; optional `run advance` when host is not running — no worker, no receipt orchestration |

No step judgment file, no `instructions` in factory-flow, no `allow.cli`. Legacy `intake-checker.execute` is unbound. Blocked validation seals intake only (no transition).

## Execute intake gate (`execute.intake.gate` — engine decider, no worker)

| Owner | Responsibility |
|---|---|
| Engine | `on_examine` checks on sealed `execute.intake`; `resolve_engine_gate` maps intake receipt `passed` → decision `pass`, seal, route to `execute.branch` |
| Steward / host | `run advance` when not auto-advancing; read `reads.intake_receipt` in context if blocked — no `gate decide` |

No worker, no `judgment.md` — gate instructions only (`instructions.md`). Markdown context includes `## Intake evidence` from the sealed intake receipt summary.

## Execute branch (`execute.branch` — engine-owned)

| Owner | Responsibility |
|---|---|
| Engine | `on_examine` `prior-execute-intake-sealed`; `run_execute_branch_complete` on `run advance` when opened: branch name, git checkout/create, branch + `execution_graph_id` state, transition to `execute.plan` |
| Steward | Optional `run advance` when host is not running — no manual branch creation on the happy path |

No step judgment file, no `instructions` in factory-flow, no `allow.cli`. Markdown context includes `## Feature branch` engine-owned blurb (no Instructions/Judgment sections).

## Registry sync (same change)

When adding or changing steward CLI in a step file, update the node in `.cursor/foundry/flows/factory-flow.yaml`:

| Step adds… | Update in YAML |
|---|---|
| `visit state patch` | `allow.cli`: `visit.state_patch`; `allow.state`: patched paths |
| `ledger show` | `allow.cli`: `ledger.show` |
| `artifact publish` | `allow.cli`: `artifact.publish`; `produces` + `allow.files.write` |
| `receipt seal` | `allow.cli`: `receipt.link`; `receipts` schemas |
| `visit transition` | `allow.cli`: `transition` |
| Receipt/artifact draft paths | `allow.files.write` for each path written before seal |

Do **not** add `allow.cli` for engine hooks (`app validate`, catalog checks) or product bootstrap (`run create`, `run context --markdown`, `cli resolve`).

Do **not** change `instructions:` unless deliberately rebinding a different step file.

When `allow.cli` changes, update acceptance features under `.cursor/foundry/cli/tests/acceptance/features/` and run `foundry dev acceptance`.

## Engine domain — keep out of step files

Lifecycle states, hook names, catalog check ids, connection selection, admission source, and links to node reference docs.

Steward **may** read ledger events when assembling **intake-receipt** evidence — that is not re-running hooks. Agent-receipt step instructions do not include `ledger show`.

## Anti-patterns

| Anti-pattern | Fix |
|---|---|
| "Contract in factory-flow.yaml" header | Delete |
| Steward drafts ticket then re-drafts from worker | Worker proposes; steward writes once |
| ` ```text ` / shell fences for foundry argv | `foundry-invoke` |
| Hook names in steward text | On intake nodes: "ledger `check.recorded` for this visit" |
| `ledger show --visit` | Filter by `visit_id` in assembly |
| Inlined receipt JSON field recipes | "Build draft per `registry:schemas/…`" |
| Catalog check ids in Boundaries | Plain-language prohibition |
| Step > 80 lines | Trim; reference schemas |
| Steward CLI without `allow.cli` update | Registry sync in same change |
| Separate `instructions_path` read after markdown packet | Follow inlined `## Instructions` |

## Before merge

- [ ] ≤ 80 lines; `foundry-invoke` fences; packet placeholders
- [ ] Goal has no routing target; boundaries have no catalog check ids
- [ ] Evidence order and branch CLI fences complete
- [ ] `allow.cli` / `allow.state` / `allow.files.write` match the step
- [ ] `foundry dev acceptance` passes
